# ===== AI agent runtime state (not docs) =====

# Secrets & API keys
.claude/.env
.claude/settings.local.json
.env
*.env.local

# `.claude/settings.json` used to be ignored here too. It is small, contains no
# secrets, and is the file that makes the repo's agent configuration reproducible
# for anyone who clones it — with it ignored, a clone got zero agent config.

# Agent worktrees and locks are ephemeral.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
skills/

# ─── Docs that SHIP ───
#
# These were previously under "INTERNAL / DO NOT RELEASE", which was wrong for
# three of them:
#   * CLAUDE.md — the project's engineering guide. README and CONTRIBUTING both
#     point at it, so ignoring it meant the repo's own front matter referred to
#     a file a clone could not see.
#   * docs/design-system.md — README links to it directly. A clone got a broken
#     link on the front page.
#   * docs/design-bible*.md — the UI design rationale the implementation prompts
#     are written against.
# `plans/` and `UX/` remain ignored: they are session scratch, not documentation.

# Stitch mockups & prototypes
stitch-*.html
236/
UX/

# Build output & debug logs
src-tauri/cargo_check_output.txt
src-tauri/check_err.txt

# Test reports
tests_report*.json

# Coverage output. Generated by `pnpm test:coverage`; the HTML report is
# ~50 files of vendored JS/CSS that changes on every run and tells a reviewer
# nothing in a diff. The `coverage/` directory that was committed here has
# been untracked.
coverage/


# Throwaway typecheck harness — fully regenerated by
# tools/typecheck-harness/check.sh from src-tauri/Cargo.toml.
tools/typecheck-harness/build/

# Generated: the probe builds these four modules from src-tauri/src.
tools/crypto-probe/target/
